#+TITLE: @journalist — Mood + sentiment specialist console
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: journalist-console
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:journalist:specialist:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# Specialist console for @journalist (Mood + sentiment specialist). Designed by
# @geordi via deepseek-r1 askbook on 2026-05-07. Each chart's
# metric is verbatim from org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml.

* LLM Error Rate by Model and Outcome
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Identifies models and outcomes with higher error rates, helping to
pinpoint areas for improvement in the LLM system.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name llm_error_rate_by_model_and_outcome :metric llm_error_rate :group_by [model, outcome]
SELECT model, outcome, AVG(CASE WHEN outcome != 'ok' THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS llm_error_rate FROM llm_calls GROUP BY model, outcome
#+END_SRC

* Crew Action Success Rate by Agent and Action
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Reveals which agents and actions have higher failure rates, guiding
focus on specific agents or actions that need optimization.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name crew_action_success_rate_by_agent_and_action :metric crew_failures :group_by [agent_to, crew_action]
SELECT agent_to, action AS crew_action, SUM(CASE WHEN outcome != 'ok' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS crew_failures FROM crew_log GROUP BY agent_to, action
#+END_SRC

* Historical Event Distribution by Kind and Day
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: area
:END:

Shows the trend of different event kinds over time, providing insights
into system behavior and potential areas of concern.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name historical_event_distribution_by_kind_and_day :metric hist_kind_count :group_by [hist_kind, hist_day]
SELECT kind AS hist_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(DISTINCT kind) AS hist_kind_count FROM history GROUP BY kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Sensor Alert Rate by Probe and Day
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Tracks the alert rate of different probes over time, helping to
identify patterns or anomalies in sensor readings.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name sensor_alert_rate_by_probe_and_day :metric probe_alert_rate :group_by [probe, sensor_day]
SELECT probe, date(ts, 'unixepoch') AS sensor_day, AVG(CASE WHEN status IN ('watch','alert','critical') THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS probe_alert_rate FROM sensor_log GROUP BY probe, date(ts, 'unixepoch')
#+END_SRC
